   $q$A seat on an observation wheel has height $h(t) = 25 - 20\cos\left(\frac{\pi t}{5}\right)$ meters after $t$ minutes. What is the height of the seat at $t = \frac{10}{3}$ minutes?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$5$ meters","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-cosine-equals-one"},{"text":"$15$ meters","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-positive-cosine-value"},{"text":"$35$ meters","is_correct":true},{"text":"$25 + 10\\sqrt{3}$ meters","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-wrong-special-value"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$35$ meters$q$, $q$The argument is $\frac{\pi}{5} \cdot \frac{10}{3} = \frac{2\pi}{3}$, and $\cos\left(\frac{2\pi}{3}\right) = -\frac{1}{2}$, so $h = 25 - 20\left(-\frac{1}{2}\right) = 35$ meters. The choice $15$ meters uses $+\frac{1}{2}$ for the cosine, forgetting that $\frac{2\pi}{3}$ is in quadrant II.$q$, 'draft', null)
