  ('eba2286f-934b-53fb-adbf-34b2e6ec5b57', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'math-g11-trigonometric-functions-and-the-unit-circle'), null, 'hard',
   $q$In Lucia's town one spring day, the temperature reaches a low of $12^\circ$C at 4 a.m. and a high of $26^\circ$C at 4 p.m., following a 24 hour sinusoidal cycle. Which function gives the temperature $T$ at $t$ hours after midnight?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$T(t) = -7\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi(t - 4)}{24}\\right) + 19$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-period-in-place-of-half-period"},{"text":"$T(t) = -14\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi(t - 4)}{12}\\right) + 19$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-range-as-amplitude"},{"text":"$T(t) = 7\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi(t - 4)}{12}\\right) + 19$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"put-maximum-at-low-time"},{"text":"$T(t) = -7\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi(t - 4)}{12}\\right) + 19$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$T(t) = -7\cos\left(\frac{\pi(t - 4)}{12}\right) + 19$$q$, $q$The midline is $\frac{12 + 26}{2} = 19$, the amplitude is $\frac{26 - 12}{2} = 7$, $b = \frac{2\pi}{24} = \frac{\pi}{12}$, and $-\cos$ shifted by 4 gives the low of $12$ at $t = 4$. The choice with $+7\cos$ would make 4 a.m. the warmest time instead of the coldest.$q$, 'draft', null)
