   $q$Dmitri builds a pendulum 80 centimeters long. Its bob swings along an arc 30 centimeters long. To the nearest tenth of a degree, what angle does the pendulum sweep through?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$0.4^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-to-convert-radians-to-degrees"},{"text":"$10.7^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-double-length-as-radius"},{"text":"$152.8^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"inverted-arc-and-radius"},{"text":"$21.5^\\circ$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$21.5^\circ$$q$, $q$The angle in radians is $\theta = \frac{s}{r} = \frac{30}{80} = 0.375$, and $0.375 \cdot \frac{180}{\pi} \approx 21.5^\circ$. The choice $0.4^\circ$ reports the radian measure as if it were degrees.$q$, 'draft', null)
