   $q$An angle $\theta$ has $\cos\theta = 0.6$. What is $\cos(\theta + \pi)$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$0.6$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignored-half-turn"},{"text":"$0.6 + \\pi$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-pi-to-the-value"},{"text":"$-0.6$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$-0.4$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subtracted-from-one"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$-0.6$$q$, $q$Adding $\pi$ is a half turn, which sends the point $(x, y)$ on the unit circle to $(-x, -y)$, so $\cos(\theta + \pi) = -0.6$. The choice $0.6$ forgets that the half turn moves the point to the opposite side of the circle.$q$, 'draft', null)
